<title>POLAND: FORECAST-Polish 52-wk,13-wk T-bill yield seen down.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-Polish 52-wk,13-wk T-bill yield seen down.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banks expect the average yield on Poland's benchmark 52-week T-bill to fall to 18.66 percent at the end of 1997 against 21.45 percent at last week's primary sale, a Reuters poll of the country's 23 largest banks showed.</p>
<p>The average yield on the 13-week T-bill was also seen falling to 18.27 percent by year-end from 20.82 percent at Monday's primary auction, the poll showed.</p>
<p>But both predictions were higher than a month ago.</p>
<p>		    JUNE	   END-97	  12-MONTHS AHEAD</p>
<p> 52-WEEK AVG   21.44	18.66 (18.40)     17.41 (17.42)</p>
<p>     MINIMUM   21.00	16.30 (16.5)	14.40 (15.8)</p>
<p>     MAXIMUM   22.10	20.60 (20.6)	19.80 (21.4)</p>
<p> 13-WEEK AVG   20.87	18.27 (18.00)     16.95 (17.05)</p>
<p>     MINIMUM   20.50	16.20 (15.9)	14.10 (14.50)</p>
<p>     MAXIMUM   22.00	20.30 (20.35)     19.50 (21.2)</p>
<p>NOTE: In brackets previous figures for end-97 and May-98 from last month's poll.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
